WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.208
- Hello, Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.208 --> 00:00:07.240
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.335
that entrepreneurs are going to solve all

00:00:09.335 --> 00:00:11.441
of the world's major problems.

00:00:11.441 --> 00:00:13.149
I started the Mentor
Me series with the goal

00:00:13.149 --> 00:00:14.998
to try to learn from people who've done

00:00:14.998 --> 00:00:17.913
a lot more than us, people
who have done amazing things,

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:20.346
that by spending a little
bit more time with them,

00:00:20.346 --> 00:00:22.575
hopefully some of their
values, their belief systems,

00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:24.935
their way of thinking
seeps into us to help us

00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:27.532
become the best version of ourselves.

00:00:27.532 --> 00:00:29.738
So today we're going to
learn from Bishop T.D. Jakes

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:31.800
and some of his best motivation.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.278
Mentor me, Bishop Jakes.

00:00:33.278 --> 00:00:34.848
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:34.848 --> 00:00:37.125
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:37.125 --> 00:00:38.572
And as always, guys, as you're watching,

00:00:38.572 --> 00:00:40.798
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:40.798 --> 00:00:42.592
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:42.592 --> 00:00:44.399
and put quotes around
it so other people can

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:47.058
be inspired as well, and
when you write it down,

00:00:47.058 --> 00:00:51.521
it's much more likely to stick
with yourself too, enjoy.

00:00:51.521 --> 00:00:54.271
(dramatic music)

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:06.853
- Life demands that you pick up the pace.

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:10.320
If you don't pick up the pace,
you're going to be left behind.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.249
I'm amazed at the people
that lack the flexibility

00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:17.380
to pick up the pace,
they just get in a rut.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.875
I stroll down here and
I'm going to stroll back.

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:25.623
I'm going to stroll over here,
I'm going to stroll over there.

00:01:25.623 --> 00:01:28.576
One of the most amazing
things about the disaster

00:01:28.576 --> 00:01:30.667
at Malaysia is that when it happened,

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.337
everybody had to pick up the pace.

00:01:33.337 --> 00:01:35.692
All the news media had
to pick up the pace.

00:01:35.692 --> 00:01:38.065
They were booking night
flights and flying over here

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:39.163
and flying over there.

00:01:39.163 --> 00:01:40.472
Somebody had to work overtime.

00:01:40.472 --> 00:01:42.711
Won't be home for three
days, typing in the middle

00:01:42.711 --> 00:01:44.526
of the night, research going on.

00:01:44.526 --> 00:01:46.398
Because when something happens,

00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:48.907
everybody got to pick up the pace.

00:01:48.907 --> 00:01:51.798
That's why I can't deal with people

00:01:51.798 --> 00:01:54.277
who cannot pick up the pace.

00:01:54.277 --> 00:01:58.708
Don't be strollin' when
I got a 9-1-1 on you.

00:01:58.708 --> 00:02:01.884
I need people who can pick up the pace.

00:02:01.884 --> 00:02:05.884
(cheers and applause)

00:02:05.884 --> 00:02:07.978
Slap your neighbor and
say pick up the pace!

00:02:07.978 --> 00:02:09.185
- [Audience] Pick up the pace!

00:02:09.185 --> 00:02:11.585
- Something's about to
happen, pick up the pace,

00:02:11.585 --> 00:02:13.704
something is about to
happen, pick up the pace,

00:02:13.704 --> 00:02:15.826
something is about to
happen, pick up the pace,

00:02:15.826 --> 00:02:18.142
something is about to
happen, pick up the pace,

00:02:18.142 --> 00:02:20.385
something is about to
happen, pick up the pace,

00:02:20.385 --> 00:02:21.899
something is about to happen.

00:02:21.899 --> 00:02:24.323
I came to tell the young
people, pick up the pace,

00:02:24.323 --> 00:02:26.558
pick up the pace, pick up the pace!

00:02:26.558 --> 00:02:28.781
Something is about to happen!

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.235
The danger of low expectations.

00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:34.276
(groans and applause)

00:02:34.276 --> 00:02:38.457
I would rather aim for
the stars and not hit them

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:41.003
than to not aim at all.

00:02:41.003 --> 00:02:43.911
I would rather go after it and not get it,

00:02:43.911 --> 00:02:46.195
than not go after it at all.

00:02:46.195 --> 00:02:50.413
I'd rather try and fail,
than not try at all.

00:02:50.413 --> 00:02:52.503
I don't want to live with the idea,

00:02:52.503 --> 00:02:54.386
wonder what would have happened

00:02:54.386 --> 00:02:56.697
had I done more with my life.

00:02:56.697 --> 00:03:01.241
I'm going to go for it,
come hell or high water.

00:03:01.241 --> 00:03:04.200
I'm going after my destiny.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.554
Touch your neighbor and say run!

00:03:06.554 --> 00:03:07.831
- [Audience] Run!

00:03:07.831 --> 00:03:10.502
- You got to run after your destiny.

00:03:10.502 --> 00:03:13.134
You can't stroll after your destiny.

00:03:13.134 --> 00:03:17.793
You can't walk after your
destiny, you got to run!

00:03:17.793 --> 00:03:19.868
Somebody holler run!

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.285
- [Audience] Run!

00:03:26.397 --> 00:03:30.230
- You got to run, you got
to run, you got to run.

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:32.588
You can't just wake up in the morning,

00:03:32.588 --> 00:03:35.193
let me see what's going to happen today.

00:03:35.193 --> 00:03:37.386
I don't know what I'ma do, I don't know

00:03:37.386 --> 00:03:39.881
what I'ma wear, I don't
know what I'm going to cook,

00:03:39.881 --> 00:03:43.089
I don't know where I'm
going to go, I just woke up.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.243
Oh, you should stay in the bed.

00:03:45.243 --> 00:03:48.322
Give the day to somebody
who's going to run

00:03:48.322 --> 00:03:49.875
after their destiny.

00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:52.767
Give the day to somebody who has a plan,

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:57.067
who has a strategy, because
success is never an accident.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:04:00.192
And if you don't want
it, get out of my way.

00:04:00.192 --> 00:04:03.849
Because there are some people
who want to do something

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:07.062
with their life who will run.

00:04:07.062 --> 00:04:09.723
Paul writes to Timothy and says,

00:04:09.723 --> 00:04:11.723
"I fought a good fight."

00:04:12.733 --> 00:04:16.579
Letting him know, "Being me is not easy."

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:18.790
It's not for the faint of heart.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.323
It's not in my suits.

00:04:21.323 --> 00:04:23.464
You can get suits like me,

00:04:23.464 --> 00:04:26.707
but they won't make you stand like me.

00:04:26.707 --> 00:04:29.040
I fought a good fight, baby.

00:04:29.994 --> 00:04:32.800
I fought one hell of a fight.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.000
Are there any fighters in here?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.836
(cheers and applause)

00:04:37.836 --> 00:04:40.710
Slap somebody and tell
them, I fought a good fight.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.219
- [Audience] I fought a good fight!

00:04:42.219 --> 00:04:44.957
- I fought my way up,
I fought to get work.

00:04:44.957 --> 00:04:46.973
I fought to get up on my feet.

00:04:46.973 --> 00:04:50.211
I fought to stand, I fought to carry on.

00:04:50.211 --> 00:04:53.270
I fought to love, I fought to live.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.185
I fought to get out the bed.

00:04:55.185 --> 00:04:59.011
I fought with my fears,
my doubts, my anxieties,

00:04:59.011 --> 00:05:03.028
my insecurities, I fought
with haters, liars,

00:05:03.028 --> 00:05:04.980
back biters and betrayers.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.569
I even had to fight with family.

00:05:07.569 --> 00:05:11.056
And many times I laid in the
bed, I couldn't go to sleep

00:05:11.056 --> 00:05:15.398
because I was fighting
with myself, I fought!

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:18.065
I know I put in it what it takes

00:05:18.965 --> 00:05:21.819
to withstand the pressure.

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:25.538
Slap your neighbor and say,
you don't know what you got.

00:05:25.538 --> 00:05:27.925
You don't know what you've got

00:05:27.925 --> 00:05:30.258
until all hell breaks loose.

00:05:31.787 --> 00:05:34.222
You don't know what you can take

00:05:34.222 --> 00:05:37.397
until the pressure is
applied to your life.

00:05:37.397 --> 00:05:39.896
You don't know what you can endure

00:05:39.896 --> 00:05:43.609
until people stab you in the
back and walk away from you.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:46.332
You don't know how much courage you have

00:05:46.332 --> 00:05:49.257
until you've been under
fire and under struggle

00:05:49.257 --> 00:05:50.871
and under tribulation.

00:05:50.871 --> 00:05:53.503
You can't learn what's in you sitting back

00:05:53.503 --> 00:05:56.295
in the Lazy-Boy chair
hitting the remote control

00:05:56.295 --> 00:05:58.355
watching HBO and Cinemax.

00:05:58.355 --> 00:06:01.038
But when all hell breaks loose,

00:06:01.038 --> 00:06:04.205
(cheers and applause)

00:06:06.307 --> 00:06:08.474
that's when you get to see

00:06:15.306 --> 00:06:16.389
what you got.

00:06:18.035 --> 00:06:20.624
Touch your neighbor and
say, I'm made of something.

00:06:20.624 --> 00:06:22.016
- [Audience] I'm made of something.

00:06:22.016 --> 00:06:25.272
- I didn't get to see the design,

00:06:25.272 --> 00:06:27.842
I didn't get to see the
architectural plans,

00:06:27.842 --> 00:06:30.594
but I know I'm made of some good stuff.

00:06:30.594 --> 00:06:33.174
I can tell by the burdens I bear

00:06:33.174 --> 00:06:36.825
and the load I carry
and the stuff I endure.

00:06:36.825 --> 00:06:40.806
I shock myself at what I'm able to take.

00:06:40.806 --> 00:06:45.040
It's not just that I shock
my enemies, I shock myself.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.564
They said I was going to
die, and I believed it.

00:06:48.564 --> 00:06:52.880
But through hell and high
water, I'm still here.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.914
To be anxious is to have
anxiety about something

00:06:55.914 --> 00:06:57.875
that hasn't even happened yet.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:01.065
Some of you are so worried
by the threat of trouble.

00:07:01.065 --> 00:07:02.823
You're not in trouble,
it's just that trouble

00:07:02.823 --> 00:07:05.228
has threatened you, and the threat of

00:07:05.228 --> 00:07:08.311
what might happen, what could happen,

00:07:11.131 --> 00:07:12.468
is wearing you down.

00:07:12.468 --> 00:07:14.573
Half of the things that you
thought were going to happen

00:07:14.573 --> 00:07:17.673
never did happen, but if
you allow those thoughts

00:07:17.673 --> 00:07:20.308
to dwell in your mind, it will succeed

00:07:20.308 --> 00:07:23.703
at robbing you of your peace,
robbing you of your joy,

00:07:23.703 --> 00:07:27.101
robbing you of your life just
because you thought yourself

00:07:27.101 --> 00:07:29.680
into a nervous breakdown,
you thought yourself

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:33.474
into depression, you thought
yourself into defeatism.

00:07:33.474 --> 00:07:35.724
The mind is a battleground.

00:07:36.603 --> 00:07:38.550
The fight is in your mind.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:42.266
So I want to challenge you
to waste no more effort

00:07:42.266 --> 00:07:44.626
wrestling with other people.

00:07:44.626 --> 00:07:47.716
(cheers and applause)

00:07:47.716 --> 00:07:50.343
Oh, I lost you, I lost you,
you were doing real good,

00:07:50.343 --> 00:07:54.204
I lost you.
(cheers and applause)

00:07:54.204 --> 00:07:58.297
Your destiny, your
future is not predicated

00:07:58.297 --> 00:08:00.964
on the decision of someone else.

00:08:02.051 --> 00:08:03.977
You wasted too much of your life trying

00:08:03.977 --> 00:08:07.985
to change other people's mind about you.

00:08:07.985 --> 00:08:11.409
It doesn't matter what
they think about you.

00:08:11.409 --> 00:08:14.180
God is not going to bless
you by their opinion.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:17.935
God is going to bless you
by how you see yourself.

00:08:17.935 --> 00:08:20.365
(cheers and applause)

00:08:20.365 --> 00:08:22.993
Touch somebody and say I
believe I'm coming out.

00:08:22.993 --> 00:08:25.555
- [Audience] I believe I'm coming out.

00:08:25.555 --> 00:08:27.425
- I don't know long it's going to take.

00:08:27.425 --> 00:08:29.700
I don't know what I'm going
to have to go through.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.872
I don't know what I'm going
to lose along the way,

00:08:31.872 --> 00:08:35.354
but I still believe that I'm coming out.

00:08:35.354 --> 00:08:38.093
I've been broke, I've
been busted and disgusted,

00:08:38.093 --> 00:08:40.817
but I still believe that I'm coming out.

00:08:40.817 --> 00:08:44.239
I'm locked up in prison,
they say I'll never get out,

00:08:44.239 --> 00:08:48.054
but I still believe that I'm coming out.

00:08:48.054 --> 00:08:50.341
I'm coming out if I don't
have nowhere to stay.

00:08:50.341 --> 00:08:53.276
I'm coming out if my husband
marries somebody else.

00:08:53.276 --> 00:08:55.826
I'm coming out if I don't have no job.

00:08:55.826 --> 00:08:57.659
I'm coming out, oh oh!

00:08:58.503 --> 00:09:02.090
I lost a lot of stuff,
I lost a lot of friends,

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:05.704
I lost a lot of strength,
I lost a lot of courage,

00:09:05.704 --> 00:09:09.107
I lost a lot of time,
I lost a lot of money,

00:09:09.107 --> 00:09:13.274
but I kept down on me knees,
I was still believing.

00:09:14.346 --> 00:09:16.481
Broke I was believing.

00:09:16.481 --> 00:09:18.530
Lonely I was believing.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.147
Betrayed I was...

00:09:20.147 --> 00:09:23.314
(cheers and applause)

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:38.277
Touch three people and
tell them keep the faith,

00:09:38.277 --> 00:09:39.110
keep the faith.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:40.453
- [Audience] Keep the faith.

00:09:40.453 --> 00:09:42.736
- If you lose your job, keep the faith.

00:09:42.736 --> 00:09:44.909
If you lose your spouse, keep the faith.

00:09:44.909 --> 00:09:47.384
If you bury your child, keep the faith.

00:09:47.384 --> 00:09:49.818
If you have to downsize, keep the faith.

00:09:49.818 --> 00:09:52.444
If you have to move in with
your mama, keep the faith.

00:09:52.444 --> 00:09:54.626
If you're at your wit's
end, keep the faith.

00:09:54.626 --> 00:09:56.902
If you have to catch
the bus, keep the faith.

00:09:56.902 --> 00:09:59.293
If you have to thumb, keep the faith.

00:09:59.293 --> 00:10:01.363
If you get sick, keep the faith.

00:10:01.363 --> 00:10:03.724
If you lose your kidneys, keep the faith.

00:10:03.724 --> 00:10:06.392
If you got heart trouble, keep the faith.

00:10:06.392 --> 00:10:08.156
You might not get a new heart,

00:10:08.156 --> 00:10:10.300
but you got to keep your faith.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.836
Have you ever noticed that when
your faith is the strongest

00:10:13.836 --> 00:10:16.555
you come up under the greatest attack?

00:10:16.555 --> 00:10:19.191
Because every time the devil
senses that you're about

00:10:19.191 --> 00:10:22.405
to walk into who you'll be, he knows next

00:10:22.405 --> 00:10:24.795
you're going to do
something, and he's trying

00:10:24.795 --> 00:10:26.774
to stop you from doing it.

00:10:26.774 --> 00:10:28.980
Slap somebody, say just do it!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.376
- [Audience] Just do it.

00:10:30.376 --> 00:10:33.146
- The enemy's trying to
stop you from doing it,

00:10:33.146 --> 00:10:36.290
because every time you
have a being moment,

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:39.468
he tries to detour you,
because as soon as you

00:10:39.468 --> 00:10:43.551
figure out who you are,
you're going to do exploits.

00:10:44.781 --> 00:10:47.480
Slap somebody and say
I got something to do.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.958
- [Audience] I got something to do.

00:10:48.958 --> 00:10:51.041
- That's why all hell is
breaking loose in my life.

00:10:51.041 --> 00:10:52.420
I got something to do.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.350
That's why I keep going
through storms and setbacks.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:55.876
I got something to do.

00:10:55.876 --> 00:10:57.976
That's why I keep getting sick in my body.

00:10:57.976 --> 00:10:59.689
I got something to do.

00:10:59.689 --> 00:11:02.343
That's why the devil
keeps bring up my past.

00:11:02.343 --> 00:11:04.175
Because I got something to do.

00:11:04.175 --> 00:11:06.652
That's why he's trying to break my heart.

00:11:06.652 --> 00:11:08.652
Because I got something.

00:11:10.582 --> 00:11:13.663
Oh, do you hear what I'm
teaching this morning?

00:11:13.663 --> 00:11:15.391
(cheers)

00:11:15.391 --> 00:11:19.611
Shake your neighbors hand and
say I got something to do.

00:11:19.611 --> 00:11:22.979
To be planted is destiny concealed.

00:11:22.979 --> 00:11:26.062
To have increase is destiny revealed.

00:11:28.662 --> 00:11:30.912
(applause)

00:11:31.879 --> 00:11:35.495
So when you plant a
seed, you don't plant it

00:11:35.495 --> 00:11:39.247
as if the planting were
the final destination.

00:11:39.247 --> 00:11:42.098
You plant it and you can't see it anymore.

00:11:42.098 --> 00:11:45.265
Its destiny is concealed, in the hopes

00:11:46.845 --> 00:11:50.722
that ultimately it will
become a stalk of corn

00:11:50.722 --> 00:11:53.487
or an apple tree or
whatever it was you planted.

00:11:53.487 --> 00:11:56.500
And in between the destiny concealed

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:00.667
and the destiny revealed is
something we call watering.

00:12:04.031 --> 00:12:07.781
And I thought, as dynamic
as the text may be,

00:12:09.912 --> 00:12:13.579
to grapple with the
notion of being planted,

00:12:14.519 --> 00:12:18.435
and to grapple with the
notion of having increase

00:12:18.435 --> 00:12:21.659
seems totally irrelevant, if we don't stop

00:12:21.659 --> 00:12:23.909
by the station of watering.

00:12:25.395 --> 00:12:29.562
Because watering is the
last step before increase.

00:12:32.563 --> 00:12:36.730
It is the transition point
between what is concealed

00:12:38.094 --> 00:12:40.676
and what is revealed.

00:12:40.676 --> 00:12:43.472
And without the benefit of watering,

00:12:43.472 --> 00:12:46.978
the destiny will die in the ground,

00:12:46.978 --> 00:12:50.134
never reaching its
potential simply because

00:12:50.134 --> 00:12:51.798
it has never been watered.

00:12:51.798 --> 00:12:54.093
And I thought I would
ask you this morning,

00:12:54.093 --> 00:12:55.941
have you ever been watered?

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:58.401
I'm reading somebody's mail right now.

00:12:58.401 --> 00:13:01.354
(laughter)

00:13:01.354 --> 00:13:04.056
You cannot embrace what
I'm about to teach,

00:13:04.056 --> 00:13:07.401
if you don't understand
that you have been planted.

00:13:07.401 --> 00:13:11.754
You didn't grow wild,
you didn't just happen,

00:13:11.754 --> 00:13:13.943
you weren't just an afterthought,

00:13:13.943 --> 00:13:18.336
you didn't just come to
be, you were planted.

00:13:18.336 --> 00:13:20.709
The sperm cell that created you

00:13:20.709 --> 00:13:23.731
out swam all of the
millions of other cells

00:13:23.731 --> 00:13:26.085
before you had a Bible.

00:13:26.085 --> 00:13:28.335
(applause)

00:13:29.265 --> 00:13:32.906
Before you had a Bible,
before you had a hymn book,

00:13:32.906 --> 00:13:34.995
you were already in a fight,

00:13:34.995 --> 00:13:37.332
and that cell out swam all the rest

00:13:37.332 --> 00:13:39.835
because you have been planted.

00:13:39.835 --> 00:13:43.002
(cheers and applause)

00:13:46.272 --> 00:13:48.498
I want to make the distinction
about being planted,

00:13:48.498 --> 00:13:51.447
because the act of
planting can be confusing

00:13:51.447 --> 00:13:54.051
to the student who has not watched.

00:13:54.051 --> 00:13:58.051
Because planting looks
no different from burial.

00:14:00.126 --> 00:14:02.376
(applause)

00:14:06.408 --> 00:14:08.046
In order to do either one of them,

00:14:08.046 --> 00:14:10.213
you got to do some digging.

00:14:11.791 --> 00:14:14.065
And once you dig down in the ground,

00:14:14.065 --> 00:14:16.315
both of them are concealed.

00:14:17.651 --> 00:14:20.151
But one of them has a destiny,

00:14:21.044 --> 00:14:23.542
and the other one does not.

00:14:23.542 --> 00:14:26.959
You bury the dead to get rid of the body,

00:14:28.384 --> 00:14:31.785
but you plant a seed so that it can go

00:14:31.785 --> 00:14:35.161
through a transformation of coming back up

00:14:35.161 --> 00:14:38.044
greater than it was when it went down.

00:14:38.044 --> 00:14:39.763
Oh good God of mercy.

00:14:39.763 --> 00:14:43.024
That's so good I'm going to
come over here and say it again.

00:14:43.024 --> 00:14:45.035
(cheers and applause)

00:14:45.035 --> 00:14:48.500
When you plant a seed,
you're not burying it

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.021
to get rid of it, you're planting it

00:14:51.021 --> 00:14:53.444
so that it can go through a metamorphosis

00:14:53.444 --> 00:14:57.791
and come back up better than
it was when it went down.

00:14:57.791 --> 00:15:01.623
How many people in this
room have come up better

00:15:01.623 --> 00:15:02.868
than you were?

00:15:02.868 --> 00:15:06.035
(cheers and applause)

00:15:09.237 --> 00:15:11.154
I'm better, I'm better.

00:15:12.793 --> 00:15:16.083
I'm better than I was when I went down.

00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:19.166
It was good for me that
I've been afflicted.

00:15:19.166 --> 00:15:21.006
For had I not been afflicted, I would have

00:15:21.006 --> 00:15:23.413
never known the glory of God.

00:15:23.413 --> 00:15:25.816
I'm better for it, I didn't like it,

00:15:25.816 --> 00:15:27.445
but I'm better for it.

00:15:27.445 --> 00:15:30.294
I couldn't see down there,
but I'm better for it.

00:15:30.294 --> 00:15:33.005
You see, I was planted in a dark place

00:15:33.005 --> 00:15:36.973
where my sight didn't work
for me, but I'm better for it.

00:15:36.973 --> 00:15:39.571
Every time you go through something hard

00:15:39.571 --> 00:15:41.761
and you can't see your way out,

00:15:41.761 --> 00:15:45.403
remember you've been
planted, not been buried.

00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:47.326
And when you come up.

00:15:47.326 --> 00:15:50.493
(cheers and applause)

00:15:56.674 --> 00:15:59.091
I'm coming up, I'm coming up.

00:16:00.304 --> 00:16:02.821
Brother right here on the come up.

00:16:02.821 --> 00:16:05.288
I said brother right here on the come up.

00:16:05.288 --> 00:16:07.585
Is there any sisters
in here on the come up?

00:16:07.585 --> 00:16:08.903
(cheers)

00:16:08.903 --> 00:16:11.254
Are there any families
in here on the come up?

00:16:11.254 --> 00:16:12.244
(cheers)

00:16:12.244 --> 00:16:14.018
Are there any preachers
in here on the come up?

00:16:14.018 --> 00:16:15.034
(cheers)

00:16:15.034 --> 00:16:16.679
You already been through hell,

00:16:16.679 --> 00:16:18.607
already been through high water,

00:16:18.607 --> 00:16:22.232
already been planted,
already been in a dark place,

00:16:22.232 --> 00:16:24.473
but just because I'm in a dark place,

00:16:24.473 --> 00:16:27.627
don't expect me to stay in a dark place.

00:16:27.627 --> 00:16:29.676
Brother right here on the...

00:16:29.676 --> 00:16:32.843
(cheers and applause)

00:16:39.471 --> 00:16:43.374
Write yourself a note,
I have not been buried,

00:16:43.374 --> 00:16:45.041
I have been planted.

00:16:46.061 --> 00:16:50.055
I may be underground, but
I'm not buried in this mess,

00:16:50.055 --> 00:16:53.365
I'm planted in it, I'm planted in it.

00:16:53.365 --> 00:16:57.803
And if I'm planted in it,
expect me to come back up again.

00:16:57.803 --> 00:17:01.178
And when I come back up,
you won't recognize me

00:17:01.178 --> 00:17:05.345
because I'm going to be
transformed by the experiences

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.761
that I have endured.

00:17:07.761 --> 00:17:09.260
When you talk to women about birth,

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:11.314
they immediately think
about being mothers,

00:17:11.314 --> 00:17:14.791
but I didn't come to
talk to you as mothers.

00:17:14.791 --> 00:17:17.374
I came to talk to you as babies

00:17:19.361 --> 00:17:22.028
who have outgrown the parameters

00:17:23.228 --> 00:17:25.645
of the womb that you live in.

00:17:27.797 --> 00:17:30.942
I came to talk to you as living creatures

00:17:30.942 --> 00:17:33.618
who have found restrictions in the place

00:17:33.618 --> 00:17:37.083
that you once found
nurture and nourishment

00:17:37.083 --> 00:17:41.250
and found yourself imprisoned
by narrow thinking people

00:17:43.515 --> 00:17:46.265
and narrow thinking circumstances

00:17:47.765 --> 00:17:50.313
and narrow evolving predicaments.

00:17:50.313 --> 00:17:54.925
I came to tell you that you
cannot feed in one realm

00:17:54.925 --> 00:17:57.346
and stay in that realm.

00:17:57.346 --> 00:18:00.414
That if you get enough
on the inside of you,

00:18:00.414 --> 00:18:03.170
you will find a discomfort in staying

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:06.152
in the dimension that you once lived in.

00:18:06.152 --> 00:18:09.146
And I came to prepare
your hearts and minds.

00:18:09.146 --> 00:18:13.340
If you're not prepared to
go through some bloody stuff

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:16.451
and some dirty stuff
and some stinky stuff,

00:18:16.451 --> 00:18:20.187
you don't want to keep
feeding on this kind of word.

00:18:20.187 --> 00:18:22.983
Because if you feed on this kind of word,

00:18:22.983 --> 00:18:25.967
it will open up your mind
and open up your thinking

00:18:25.967 --> 00:18:28.933
and open up your ideas
and open up your concepts

00:18:28.933 --> 00:18:32.301
until all of a sudden
you are uncomfortable

00:18:32.301 --> 00:18:34.995
in what you were once comfortable in.

00:18:34.995 --> 00:18:37.245
(applause)

00:18:40.368 --> 00:18:44.350
Some of you have already
began to experience it.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.258
You're thinking on another level,

00:18:46.258 --> 00:18:48.530
and it's causing a separation.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.996
Some of you have already
begin to experience it

00:18:50.996 --> 00:18:54.041
because what used to be
funny isn't funny anymore.

00:18:54.041 --> 00:18:56.970
And what you used to enjoy
you don't enjoy anymore.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:59.048
And what you used to be satisfied with,

00:18:59.048 --> 00:19:01.564
you're not satisfied with anymore.

00:19:01.564 --> 00:19:03.394
And all of a sudden you don't fit

00:19:03.394 --> 00:19:06.630
in the places you used to fit in.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.999
And you don't even
understand it and they think

00:19:08.999 --> 00:19:11.535
you're acting funny and they
think you're acting strange

00:19:11.535 --> 00:19:15.396
and they say things like, "You
forgot where you came from."

00:19:15.396 --> 00:19:18.879
I didn't forget it, I
just can't stay in it.

00:19:18.879 --> 00:19:22.046
(cheers and applause)

00:19:32.674 --> 00:19:36.497
Tweet that, tweet that,
I got to get out of here.

00:19:36.497 --> 00:19:38.469
I got to get out of here,
I got to get out of here,

00:19:38.469 --> 00:19:40.795
I got to get out of here,
I got to get out of here,

00:19:40.795 --> 00:19:43.747
I got to get out of here,
I've got to get out of here.

00:19:43.747 --> 00:19:47.518
You tell your twin, you can
stay in there if you want to.

00:19:47.518 --> 00:19:51.059
This might be okay for you,
but I got to get out of here.

00:19:51.059 --> 00:19:54.352
Even if I have to fight my
way out like Jacob and Esau,

00:19:54.352 --> 00:19:55.792
I've got to get out there.

00:19:55.792 --> 00:19:58.723
If I've got to pull and
tug, I've got to get out.

00:19:58.723 --> 00:20:02.883
I've got too much vision
to stay in this rut.

00:20:02.883 --> 00:20:05.082
The hardest thing to do, the
hardest thing to deal with,

00:20:05.082 --> 00:20:07.211
the hardest thing to
manage, the hardest thing

00:20:07.211 --> 00:20:09.384
to put up with is transition.

00:20:09.384 --> 00:20:11.771
The thing we hate the most is transition.

00:20:11.771 --> 00:20:13.784
We hate it because it takes
us out of our element,

00:20:13.784 --> 00:20:15.505
it takes us out of our comfort zone,

00:20:15.505 --> 00:20:17.715
it takes us out of the
place where we are secure

00:20:17.715 --> 00:20:19.758
and sure and we've learned how to manage

00:20:19.758 --> 00:20:21.134
and control everything.

00:20:21.134 --> 00:20:25.036
You cannot control everything
when you are in transition.

00:20:25.036 --> 00:20:28.345
It is what it is, it
happens like it happens.

00:20:28.345 --> 00:20:30.805
I can't get my hair done and do it.

00:20:30.805 --> 00:20:32.856
I can't be pretty about it.

00:20:32.856 --> 00:20:36.906
I got to come out any way
I can, I'm in transition.

00:20:36.906 --> 00:20:40.496
I can't meet with the board
or talk to the committee

00:20:40.496 --> 00:20:42.760
or get everybody to approve it.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:47.094
When my water breaks,
get ready, here I come.

00:20:47.094 --> 00:20:50.371
If it's under a tree,
if it's under a bush,

00:20:50.371 --> 00:20:52.265
if it's against the wall,

00:20:52.265 --> 00:20:56.432
when the water breaks,
that's my sign, here I come.

00:20:57.593 --> 00:20:59.314
Touch your neighbor and say move!

00:20:59.314 --> 00:21:00.814
- [Audience] Move!

00:21:01.961 --> 00:21:04.944
- Move, I've grown out of this spot.

00:21:04.944 --> 00:21:08.000
Move, I'm coming into another dimension.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.772
Move, I see a door opening for me.

00:21:10.772 --> 00:21:13.882
Move, I see divine permission to step.

00:21:13.882 --> 00:21:17.715
Move, I see the glory
of God calling me, move.

00:21:18.715 --> 00:21:21.715
If enough people like me, then I am.

00:21:25.093 --> 00:21:28.581
How many people following you on Twitter?

00:21:28.581 --> 00:21:30.326
I got to get my following up.

00:21:30.326 --> 00:21:31.915
I got to get my friends up.

00:21:31.915 --> 00:21:34.332
Because if I have popularity,

00:21:35.884 --> 00:21:37.574
ooh, you all got quiet again.

00:21:37.574 --> 00:21:39.781
(laughter)

00:21:39.781 --> 00:21:41.828
Let me show you how many people follow me.

00:21:41.828 --> 00:21:43.441
Do you know Bishop started following,

00:21:43.441 --> 00:21:45.430
girl, Bishop following me!

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:47.680
(laughter)

00:21:51.009 --> 00:21:55.009
So I am because of who
follows me, who likes me.

00:21:56.849 --> 00:21:59.016
Popularity-based identity.

00:22:03.353 --> 00:22:06.020
Ooh, performance-based identity.

00:22:11.253 --> 00:22:14.670
If you do this, you'll be the son of God.

00:22:16.422 --> 00:22:20.223
If they like you, you'll
be the son of God.

00:22:20.223 --> 00:22:23.285
If I give you enough
possessions, you'll be.

00:22:23.285 --> 00:22:25.868
Now, let me show you something.

00:22:26.927 --> 00:22:29.427
I'm teaching just do it, okay?

00:22:30.663 --> 00:22:33.330
And yet I'm criticizing doing it

00:22:36.562 --> 00:22:38.395
to define who you are.

00:22:42.067 --> 00:22:45.132
Well, I'm confused, should
I do it or not do it?

00:22:45.132 --> 00:22:48.993
You just said, "Just do it,"
and then you turned around

00:22:48.993 --> 00:22:52.576
and said not to define
myself by what I do.

00:22:58.622 --> 00:23:00.872
Can I critique my own text?

00:23:02.477 --> 00:23:05.132
Which way is it, Reverend?

00:23:05.132 --> 00:23:07.289
Do I do it or not do it?

00:23:07.289 --> 00:23:10.007
The problem is not about doing it,

00:23:10.007 --> 00:23:12.020
it is why you do it.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:14.632
(applause)

00:23:14.632 --> 00:23:18.644
What I am criticizing is putting the doing

00:23:18.644 --> 00:23:20.994
before the being so that you think

00:23:20.994 --> 00:23:24.100
that if I do this, I will be somebody.

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:27.212
If I buy this, I will be somebody.

00:23:27.212 --> 00:23:31.700
If they like me, I will
be, you got it backwards.

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:34.200
The people that know their God

00:23:35.709 --> 00:23:37.459
shall be and then do.

00:23:40.723 --> 00:23:42.973
(applause)

00:23:47.911 --> 00:23:50.994
And because you're doing doesn't come

00:23:51.927 --> 00:23:55.193
from the deeper place of being,

00:23:55.193 --> 00:23:57.751
it hasn't worked for you.

00:23:57.751 --> 00:24:00.288
Because you are who you are,

00:24:00.288 --> 00:24:02.900
you can do what you can do.

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:05.463
But if you're trying
to find out who you are

00:24:05.463 --> 00:24:09.045
by doing things, you will
never find out who are you

00:24:09.045 --> 00:24:12.295
by doing, you have to start with being.

00:24:14.658 --> 00:24:17.163
I want you to see this, I
don't want to lose you in this.

00:24:17.163 --> 00:24:20.336
Because the difference
between the two determines

00:24:20.336 --> 00:24:22.836
the direction of your destiny.

00:24:23.880 --> 00:24:27.030
If you're always seeking a certain status

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:31.197
to validate who you are, you're
never going to have peace.

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:34.924
You have to know who you are,

00:24:34.924 --> 00:24:37.669
and then you can climb to the status.

00:24:37.669 --> 00:24:41.248
You can't climb up to find yourself.

00:24:41.248 --> 00:24:45.821
You have to find yourself
so you can climb up.

00:24:45.821 --> 00:24:49.427
You can't climb up to find yourself.

00:24:49.427 --> 00:24:53.260
You have to find yourself
so you can climb up.

00:25:00.381 --> 00:25:02.464
So you can be who you are

00:25:04.718 --> 00:25:07.468
before anybody knows who you are.

00:25:09.638 --> 00:25:10.721
So that means

00:25:13.006 --> 00:25:16.806
you could be rich while you're broke.

00:25:16.806 --> 00:25:19.056
(applause)

00:25:22.375 --> 00:25:25.542
(cheers and applause)

00:25:28.449 --> 00:25:31.617
You could be healed while you're sick.

00:25:31.617 --> 00:25:34.630
(cheers and applause)

00:25:34.630 --> 00:25:37.797
You could be loose while you're bound.

00:25:38.806 --> 00:25:42.223
It does not yet appear what you shall be.

00:25:43.412 --> 00:25:46.405
It hasn't showed up what you shall be.

00:25:46.405 --> 00:25:49.988
But you got to be it
before you can get it.

00:25:50.864 --> 00:25:52.864
Women, thou art
- Loosed!

00:25:55.509 --> 00:25:58.428
- I know it looks like you're tied up.

00:25:58.428 --> 00:26:01.734
I know you been bowed over for 18 years.

00:26:01.734 --> 00:26:04.870
I know your conditions don't validate you.

00:26:04.870 --> 00:26:08.362
But let me tell you about who you are.

00:26:08.362 --> 00:26:11.362
You are loosed, not going to be loosed,

00:26:12.887 --> 00:26:17.454
not shall be loosed,
you're loosed on the inside

00:26:17.454 --> 00:26:20.402
before you're loosed on the outside!

00:26:20.402 --> 00:26:24.144
(cheers and applause)

00:26:24.144 --> 00:26:27.894
I'm delivered right now,
I'm whole right now!

00:26:29.324 --> 00:26:31.324
I am it, so I can do it!

00:26:33.324 --> 00:26:34.324
I can do it!

00:26:36.473 --> 00:26:39.820
I came to deliver a message
to every person in this room

00:26:39.820 --> 00:26:42.879
who's had a struggle,
who's had some pains,

00:26:42.879 --> 00:26:45.859
who's had some tests, who's
got some creative ideas

00:26:45.859 --> 00:26:48.315
but you've gone through
some really tough stuff.

00:26:48.315 --> 00:26:50.454
Let me tell you something,
the stuff you've been through,

00:26:50.454 --> 00:26:52.920
don't pay it any attention.

00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:56.943
It is just a sign that the baby is coming.

00:26:56.943 --> 00:26:59.085
You're on the verge of birthing.

00:26:59.085 --> 00:27:00.957
You're on the verge of birthing.

00:27:00.957 --> 00:27:02.646
You're on the verge of birthing.

00:27:02.646 --> 00:27:04.514
You're about to give birth.

00:27:04.514 --> 00:27:06.821
I want you to touch
everybody you can reach

00:27:06.821 --> 00:27:09.243
and tell them the baby is
coming, the baby is coming,

00:27:09.243 --> 00:27:11.786
the baby is coming, the baby is coming,

00:27:11.786 --> 00:27:14.175
the baby is coming, the baby is coming,

00:27:14.175 --> 00:27:16.617
the baby is coming, the baby is coming.

00:27:16.617 --> 00:27:19.292
You don't want to leave me
now, the baby is coming.

00:27:19.292 --> 00:27:21.699
You don't want to walk out on
me now, the baby is coming.

00:27:21.699 --> 00:27:23.890
I haven't had my best idea yet.

00:27:23.890 --> 00:27:26.204
I haven't had my most creative moment yet.

00:27:26.204 --> 00:27:28.077
I haven't produced my dream yet.

00:27:28.077 --> 00:27:30.777
I don't care whether
you're 30, 40, 50, 60, 70,

00:27:30.777 --> 00:27:33.855
there's something down inside
of you that's still kicking

00:27:33.855 --> 00:27:37.572
inside of you that wants to
get out and it wants to live!

00:27:37.572 --> 00:27:39.152
(cheers and applause)

00:27:39.152 --> 00:27:40.569
It wants to live!

00:27:41.674 --> 00:27:44.052
The whole reason you're
here today is because

00:27:44.052 --> 00:27:46.894
there's something in you
that needs to be fed,

00:27:46.894 --> 00:27:50.257
that needs to be stirred,
that needs to be electrified,

00:27:50.257 --> 00:27:52.060
that needs to be illuminated.

00:27:52.060 --> 00:27:56.439
There's something down inside
of you crying, "Let me out!"

00:27:56.439 --> 00:27:58.917
(cheers and applause)

00:27:58.917 --> 00:28:02.784
Let me out, make some noise in this place!

00:28:02.784 --> 00:28:05.951
(cheers and applause)

00:28:07.517 --> 00:28:08.684
Yes, yes, yes!

00:28:10.404 --> 00:28:12.885
We are waiting on your water to break

00:28:12.885 --> 00:28:15.896
and for you to give birth
to the greatest idea

00:28:15.896 --> 00:28:20.509
you have ever had, make
some noise in this place!

00:28:20.509 --> 00:28:23.676
(cheers and applause)

00:28:26.573 --> 00:28:29.917
Anybody who left you is going to miss it.

00:28:29.917 --> 00:28:31.766
They're going to miss
it, they're going to miss

00:28:31.766 --> 00:28:35.232
the greatest part of you, the
greatest part of your destiny,

00:28:35.232 --> 00:28:37.409
the greatest part of your creativity.

00:28:37.409 --> 00:28:40.065
It took everything you
went through yesterday

00:28:40.065 --> 00:28:43.138
to get you ready for what
you are about to do today.

00:28:43.138 --> 00:28:46.524
You are standing on the
verge of a great awakening

00:28:46.524 --> 00:28:48.174
or you wouldn't be here.

00:28:48.174 --> 00:28:51.389
If I'm talking to you, make
some noise in this place.

00:28:51.389 --> 00:28:54.556
(cheers and applause)

00:29:00.067 --> 00:29:02.033
I can't hear you!

00:29:02.033 --> 00:29:05.200
(cheers and applause)

00:29:06.954 --> 00:29:08.823
I believe there are businesses in you,

00:29:08.823 --> 00:29:11.508
companies in you, concepts in you,

00:29:11.508 --> 00:29:14.949
books to be written,
paintings to be drawn,

00:29:14.949 --> 00:29:18.682
concepts to be birthed,
ideas, creative concepts.

00:29:18.682 --> 00:29:22.693
There's something that you
could do, that you could think

00:29:22.693 --> 00:29:25.360
in your life that would
radically change your life.

00:29:25.360 --> 00:29:28.390
Somebody could take the
hand you've been dealt

00:29:28.390 --> 00:29:32.679
and win with it, same
circumstances, same ideas,

00:29:32.679 --> 00:29:37.055
they would do it through what
they thought about your life.

00:29:37.055 --> 00:29:41.131
But we don't need somebody,
because we got you.

00:29:41.131 --> 00:29:43.381
We got you, you're the one.

00:29:44.794 --> 00:29:47.989
You are the one.
(applause)

00:29:47.989 --> 00:29:51.032
I want you to join hands with
somebody for just a minute.

00:29:51.032 --> 00:29:54.014
I'm telling you right
now, if you are going

00:29:54.014 --> 00:29:56.847
to birth your dream, your calling,

00:29:59.326 --> 00:30:03.037
your passion and the
second half of your life,

00:30:03.037 --> 00:30:05.935
you can't draw back when life gets tough.

00:30:05.935 --> 00:30:09.928
You've got to stand up to it and push.

00:30:09.928 --> 00:30:12.261
Get that person by the hand,

00:30:13.121 --> 00:30:15.048
because there's something inside of them

00:30:15.048 --> 00:30:17.606
that is about to happen.

00:30:17.606 --> 00:30:19.189
Squeeze their hand.

00:30:21.854 --> 00:30:25.648
And when I count to
three, I want every man

00:30:25.648 --> 00:30:28.717
and every woman that's got a
concept, that's got an idea,

00:30:28.717 --> 00:30:31.972
I want you to push with all of your might

00:30:31.972 --> 00:30:34.930
until dreams and concepts and ideas

00:30:34.930 --> 00:30:37.049
start to birth out of you
in the middle of the night.

00:30:37.049 --> 00:30:40.155
You going to need pens and
pads by your bed tonight

00:30:40.155 --> 00:30:41.687
because you're going to
have to get up in the middle

00:30:41.687 --> 00:30:43.119
of the night and starting writing down

00:30:43.119 --> 00:30:46.175
all the stuff that's going to
start coming out of your spirit

00:30:46.175 --> 00:30:48.715
when this day is ready, are you ready?

00:30:48.715 --> 00:30:50.125
(cheers)

00:30:50.125 --> 00:30:50.958
One,

00:30:51.904 --> 00:30:52.737
two,

00:30:54.218 --> 00:30:55.368
three.

00:30:55.368 --> 00:30:57.451
(cheers)

00:31:02.881 --> 00:31:06.908
If you push it, you can
have it, God bless you!

00:31:06.908 --> 00:31:09.417
It's yours for the taking!

00:31:09.417 --> 00:31:12.584
(cheers and applause)

00:31:17.316 --> 00:31:19.694
- Thank you guys so much for
watching, I hope you enjoyed.

00:31:19.694 --> 00:31:21.576
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video

00:31:21.576 --> 00:31:24.081
that you're going to
immediately apply somehow

00:31:24.081 --> 00:31:26.006
to your life or to your business.

00:31:26.006 --> 00:31:27.353
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:31:27.353 --> 00:31:28.723
I'm super curious to find out.

00:31:28.723 --> 00:31:30.950
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Surge Wisdom.

00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:32.920
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:31:32.920 --> 00:31:35.780
Your One Word, and doing
that animated chapter review

00:31:35.780 --> 00:31:37.573
on your YouTube channel, I really, really,

00:31:37.573 --> 00:31:39.094
really appreciate your support, man.

00:31:39.094 --> 00:31:41.582
And I'm so glad that you enjoyed the read.

00:31:41.582 --> 00:31:43.953
Thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you

00:31:43.953 --> 00:31:45.976
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:31:45.976 --> 00:31:49.215
And whatever your one word is, much love.

00:31:49.215 --> 00:31:50.715
I'll see you soon.

00:31:57.209 --> 00:32:01.042
- Always go to something
bigger than yourself.

00:32:03.923 --> 00:32:06.117
I'm wondering if you've been defeated

00:32:06.117 --> 00:32:08.877
because you have been
giving yourself wholly

00:32:08.877 --> 00:32:11.845
to something that was
too small to hold you.

00:32:11.845 --> 00:32:13.928
(cheers)

00:32:16.892 --> 00:32:20.809
Have you thrust yourself
into a glass of water?

00:32:22.629 --> 00:32:24.976
Have you leaped off the diving board

00:32:24.976 --> 00:32:27.143
into a cereal bowl person?

00:32:30.935 --> 00:32:34.268
Are you not guilty of immersing yourself

00:32:35.274 --> 00:32:39.441
into things that were too
small to hold your vision?

00:32:44.959 --> 00:32:48.187
Oh my God, this so good I'm
going to get the CD myself.

00:32:48.187 --> 00:32:50.437
(laughter)

00:32:52.378 --> 00:32:56.211
Jesus sent him to throw
himself into something

00:32:57.370 --> 00:33:00.287
that was bigger than his condition.

00:33:01.374 --> 00:33:03.805
And he had to go to get to it.

00:33:03.805 --> 00:33:06.490
He had to get out of his comfort zone.

00:33:06.490 --> 00:33:10.657
My problem is, so many times
you've thrown big ideas

00:33:11.523 --> 00:33:15.190
at small people, you've
given big commitment

00:33:16.832 --> 00:33:18.665
to cereal bowl people.

00:33:19.545 --> 00:33:21.854
And you're trying to get your sight back

00:33:21.854 --> 00:33:25.271
from a source that's too small to support

00:33:26.956 --> 00:33:29.637
what you're willing to put in.

00:33:29.637 --> 00:33:33.803
Is your investment bigger than the bank?

00:33:33.803 --> 00:33:36.470
(laughing) You should see
the way you're looking at me.

00:33:36.470 --> 00:33:40.819
Is the reason you keep
being disappointed by people

00:33:40.819 --> 00:33:43.105
is that you have wholly thrown yourself

00:33:43.105 --> 00:33:45.938
into something that was too small?

00:33:50.146 --> 00:33:54.313
Jesus sends him to something
that is bigger than himself

00:33:55.627 --> 00:33:57.627
so he can wash his eyes.

00:34:01.010 --> 00:34:04.343
Are you trying to take a bath in a bowl?

